Ladybird writes what pages log to stderr, with the control characters
in it written as escapes. The other engines write the console of a
page to stderr as it is, but only when asked to: Firefox writes it
with fputs() when the devtools.console.stdout.content pref is on,
which it isn’t by default, and Chrome hands it to its logging in
LogConsoleMessage(), which reaches stderr when logging is enabled,
e.g. with --enable-logging=stderr. And WebKit’s ConsoleClient::
printConsoleMessage() writes it unescaped as well. All of this comes
from reading their sources, not from running them.
